        "message": "LU-21029 tests: stop resumed OST LFSCK in sanity-lfsck 32a\n\ntest_32a stops ost1 while its layout LFSCK is scanning, so the OST\nsaves it as paused and resumes it alone when ost1 is mounted again.\nThe test then ends with that LFSCK still running. On ZFS it can run\nfor more than a minute, and a following \"lfsck_start -o\" (test_33)\ngets -EBUSY from ost1, because the resumed LFSCK keeps no orphan\ndata. Every MDT then skips OST0000 and its layout LFSCK finishes as\n\"partial\", so the wait for \"completed\" times out.\n\nWait for ost1 to resume the LFSCK, then stop it before test_32a\nreturns.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-lfsck\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-lfsck\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I466f7844799c1c29e64be8d45dcf7f551b8b4c2f\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70634\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
